N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNEXPECTED_TOKEN, "N00B-P0001", ERROR,
    "a token appears where the grammar does not allow it",
    "The parser reached a token that cannot continue the construct it was\n"
    "reading. The message names the token, the construct, and what could\n"
    "have appeared instead. Check for a missing operator, comma or bracket\n"
    "just before the token, for example `let x = 1 2` needs `1 + 2`.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNEXPECTED_END, "N00B-P0002", ERROR,
    "the file ends in the middle of a construct",
    "The file ended while a declaration, statement or expression was still\n"
    "incomplete. Finish the construct the message names, for example by\n"
    "adding the missing expression after `=`.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNCLOSED_DELIMITER, "N00B-P0003", ERROR,
    "a `{`, `(` or `[` is never closed",
    "Every opening bracket needs a matching closing bracket. The message\n"
    "points at the bracket that is still open when the file ends. When a\n"
    "closing `}` lines up with an outer block instead of its own, the inner\n"
    "block is usually the one missing its `}`.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNMATCHED_CLOSER, "N00B-P0004", ERROR,
    "a closing bracket has no matching opening bracket",
    "A `}`, `)` or `]` appears without an open bracket of the same kind\n"
    "before it, or while a different kind of bracket is still open. Remove\n"
    "the stray bracket or add the opening bracket it was meant to close.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD, "N00B-P0005", ERROR,
    "a statement starts with a misspelled keyword",
    "A statement begins with a name that is close to a keyword, followed by\n"
    "something that cannot follow a name. This is usually a typo such as\n"
    "`fucn main()` for `func main()`.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_BLANK_LINE_IN_STATEMENT, "N00B-P0006", ERROR,
    "a statement continues across a blank line",
    "A statement may continue onto the next line, but a blank line always\n"
    "ends it. The statement before the blank line is incomplete. Finish it\n"
    "on its own lines, or remove the blank line.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_COMMENT_IN_STATEMENT, "N00B-P0007", ERROR,
    "a statement continues past a line with a comment",
    "A line that carries a comment cannot be continued on the next line.\n"
    "Finish the statement on the commented line, or move the comment.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_UNEXPECTED_INDENT, "N00B-P0008", ERROR,
    "a line is indented where no block starts",
    "Indentation opens a block only after a `:` at the end of a line.\n"
    "Indent the line like the statement before it, or start a block.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_MISPLACED_PASS, "N00B-P0009", ERROR,
    "`pass` appears somewhere other than an empty body",
    "`pass` stands for an empty body of a block, case branch, context,\n"
    "package or union. It cannot appear next to other statements or inside\n"
    "an expression.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_COMPTIME_BLOCK, "N00B-P0010", ERROR,
    "`comptime` is used as a block keyword",
    "`comptime` is a function that reports whether code runs at build time.\n"
    "Write `if comptime() { ... } else { ... }` instead of `comptime { }`.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_UNTERMINATED_STRING, "N00B-L0001", ERROR,
    "a string or character literal is not closed",
    "A quoted literal must end with its closing quote on the same line.\n"
    "Add the missing quote, or write a line break inside the string as\n"
    "`\\n`.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_UNTERMINATED_COMMENT, "N00B-L0002", ERROR,
    "a block comment is not closed",
    "A comment that starts with `/*` must end with `*/`. The file ended\n"
    "before the comment was closed.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_INVALID_ESCAPE, "N00B-L0003", ERROR,
    "a string contains an escape sequence that does not exist",
    "Valid escapes are `\\a`, `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\v`, `\\0`,\n"
    "`\\\\`, `\\\"`, `\\'`, `\\xHH`, `\\uHHHH` and `\\UHHHHHHHH`. Write a literal\n"
    "backslash as `\\\\`.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_MALFORMED_NUMBER, "N00B-L0004", ERROR,
    "a number literal is malformed",
    "A number is digits with optional `_` separators, a decimal point and\n"
    "an exponent, or `0x` followed by hexadecimal digits. Letters directly\n"
    "after the digits are not allowed: write `12 abc`, not `12abc`.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_IDENTIFIER_NOT_NFC, "N00B-L0005", ERROR,
    "an identifier is not in Unicode normalization form C",
    "Identifiers must be written in NFC so that names that look the same\n"
    "are the same. The message shows the normalized spelling to use.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_IDENTIFIER_SCRIPT, "N00B-L0006", ERROR,
    "an identifier mixes writing systems or uses a disallowed character",
    "An identifier may not combine letters from different scripts, contain\n"
    "emoji, or contain invalid UTF-8. Rename it using one script.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_TAB_INDENT, "N00B-L0007", ERROR,
    "a line is indented with tabs or with a mix of tabs and spaces",
    "n00b indents with spaces only. Replace the tabs with spaces.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_INCONSISTENT_DEDENT, "N00B-L0008", ERROR,
    "a line is dedented to a level no enclosing block uses",
    "When a line is indented less than the one before it, its indentation\n"
    "must match an enclosing block exactly. Line it up with that block.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_UNEXPECTED_CHARACTER, "N00B-L0009", ERROR,
    "the source contains a character that starts no token",
    "The character cannot begin any name, number, operator or literal.\n"
    "Remove it, or put it inside a string literal.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_CHARACTER_LITERAL_LENGTH, "N00B-L0010", ERROR,
    "a character literal does not hold exactly one character",
    "A literal in single quotes such as `'a'` holds one character. Use\n"
    "double quotes for a string.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_BIDI_CONTROL, "N00B-L0011", ERROR,
    "the source contains an invisible bidirectional control character",
    "Bidirectional control characters can make code display differently\n"
    "from how it compiles, so they are not allowed in source text. A string\n"
    "literal can write one as an escape such as `\\u202E`.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_BIDI_CONTROL_IN_FENCE, "N00B-L0012", WARNING,
    "a fenced text block contains an invisible bidirectional control",
    "The fenced block keeps the character, but it can make the text display\n"
    "differently from its contents.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_UNTERMINATED_FENCE, "N00B-L0013", ERROR,
    "a fenced text block is not closed",
    "A fenced block that starts with `[---` must end with a matching\n"
    "closing fence before the end of the file.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_INVALID_TOKEN, "N00B-L0014", ERROR,
    "the source contains text that forms no valid token",
    "The text cannot be read as a name, number, operator or literal. The\n"
    "message describes what is wrong with it.")
N00B_DIAG(LEX_SOURCE_WARNING, "N00B-L0015", WARNING,
    "the source contains text that is accepted but discouraged",
    "The message describes the problem. The program still compiles.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_MIXED_SPELLING, "N00B-P0011", WARNING,
    "a file spells the same construct in two different ways",
    "n00b accepts several spellings for some constructs, such as `{ }` or\n"
    "`:` with indentation for blocks, and `&&` or `and`. Within one file,\n"
    "pick one spelling. `--syntax-preference CLASS=SPELLING` sets the\n"
    "preferred one, and `--no-syntax-warnings` turns these warnings off.")
N00B_DIAG(SYNTAX_NONPREFERRED_SPELLING, "N00B-P0012", WARNING,
    "a construct uses a spelling other than the preferred one",
    "The file consistently uses a spelling that is not the preferred one.\n"
    "Use the suggested spelling, or set your preference with\n"
    "`--syntax-preference CLASS=SPELLING`.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPILE_ERROR_CALLED, "N00B-P0013", ERROR,
    "a `compile_error` call was reached while compiling",
    "`compile_error(\"message\")` stops the build with your message when the\n"
    "compiler evaluates it, usually inside a `when` branch that rejects an\n"
    "unsupported configuration.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPILE_WARNING_CALLED, "N00B-P0014", WARNING,
    "a `compile_warning` call was reached while compiling",
    "`compile_warning(\"message\")` prints your message as a warning when the\n"
    "compiler evaluates it. The build continues.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_EXPRESSION_FORM, "N00B-P0015", ERROR,
    "an expression that is evaluated while compiling uses a form it cannot",
    "`when` conditions and other compile-time expressions may use literals,\n"
    "`const` names, compile-time functions such as `target_os()`, and\n"
    "arithmetic, comparison and logical operators. Member access, indexing,\n"
    "casts, references and literal modifiers are not available there.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_INTEGER_RANGE, "N00B-P0016", ERROR,
    "an integer in a compile-time expression is out of range",
    "Compile-time integers are 128-bit signed values. Use a smaller value.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_FLOAT_RANGE, "N00B-P0017", ERROR,
    "a floating-point number in a compile-time expression is out of range",
    "Compile-time floating-point values are 64-bit. Use a value that fits.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_AMBIGUOUS_NAME, "N00B-P0018", ERROR,
    "a name in a compile-time expression refers to more than one module",
    "Several imported modules provide a `const` or module with this name.\n"
    "Qualify the name with its module path, for example `config.DEBUG`.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_NOT_CONST, "N00B-P0019", ERROR,
    "a compile-time expression uses a value that is not a compile-time const",
    "Only `const` declarations whose initializers are themselves\n"
    "compile-time expressions can be used in `when` conditions and other\n"
    "compile-time expressions. Variables cannot.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_BUILTIN_ARITY, "N00B-P0020", ERROR,
    "a compile-time function is called with the wrong number of arguments",
    "Functions such as `target_os()` take no arguments, and functions such\n"
    "as `preproc_value(\"NAME\")` take exactly one. Check the call.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_BUILTIN_ARGUMENT, "N00B-P0021", ERROR,
    "a compile-time function needs a string argument",
    "`compile_error`, `compile_warning`, `preproc_value` and similar\n"
    "functions take one string literal or string `const`.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_UNKNOWN_FUNCTION, "N00B-P0022", ERROR,
    "a compile-time expression calls a function that is not available there",
    "Only the compile-time functions, such as `target_os()`, `target_arch()`\n"
    "and `preproc_value()`, can be called in `when` conditions and other\n"
    "compile-time expressions.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_TARGET_QUERY_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-P0023", ERROR,
    "a compile-time target query has no answer for the current target",
    "Some target queries are only defined for some platforms. Guard the\n"
    "call with a `when` on `target_os()` or `target_arch()`.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_NO_SOURCE_DIR, "N00B-P0024", ERROR,
    "`source_dir()` is used in a module that has no source file",
    "Generated modules have no directory. Use `source_dir()` only in modules\n"
    "that come from files.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_UNDEFINED_VALUE, "N00B-P0025", ERROR,
    "`preproc_value` asks for a value that was not supplied",
    "Supply the value on the command line with `--define NAME=VALUE`, or\n"
    "check `preproc_defines(\"NAME\")` before reading it.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_DEFINE_RANGE, "N00B-P0026", ERROR,
    "a value supplied with `--define` is out of range",
    "Integers supplied with `--define` must fit in 128 bits and\n"
    "floating-point values in 64 bits.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_OPERAND_TYPE, "N00B-P0027", ERROR,
    "a compile-time operator is applied to values of the wrong type",
    "Arithmetic needs numbers, logical operators need `bool`, and both sides\n"
    "of a comparison must have the same type.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPTIME_OVERFLOW, "N00B-P0028", ERROR,
    "compile-time arithmetic overflows",
    "Compile-time integer arithmetic is checked 128-bit arithmetic; the\n"
    "result does not fit, or the expression divides by zero.")
N00B_DIAG(WHEN_CONDITION_NOT_BOOL, "N00B-P0029", ERROR,
    "a `when` condition is not a `bool`",
    "`when` selects code while compiling, so its condition must be a\n"
    "compile-time `bool`, for example `when target_os() == \"linux\" { }`.")
N00B_DIAG(MODULE_LITERAL_PLACEMENT, "N00B-P0030", ERROR,
    "a module literal is used somewhere other than a module-level `const`",
    "A module literal such as an `'ffi` block generates a module, so it can\n"
    "only initialize one `const` declared at module level:\n"
    "`const zlib = 'ffi[--- ... ---]`.")
N00B_DIAG(LITMOD_UNKNOWN_KIND, "N00B-P0031", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier names a literal kind that does not exist",
    "A literal modifier is declared as `<kind> litmod <name>`, where kind is\n"
    "a literal kind such as `string`, `int`, `float`, `list` or `record`.")
N00B_DIAG(LITMOD_DUPLICATE, "N00B-P0032", ERROR,
    "a module declares the same literal modifier twice",
    "Each module may declare one literal modifier per name and literal kind.\n"
    "Remove or rename one of the declarations.")
N00B_DIAG(INVALID_SYNTAX_PREFERENCE, "N00B-P0033", ERROR,
    "a `--syntax-preference` value is not a known class and spelling",
    "Write `--syntax-preference CLASS=SPELLING`, for example\n"
    "`--syntax-preference blocks={}`.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_NOT_FOUND, "N00B-M0001", ERROR,
    "an imported module cannot be found",
    "The module is not in the current directory, in a package root on\n"
    "`N00B_PATH`, or in the toolchain library. The message lists the places\n"
    "searched. Check the spelling, or add the directory that holds it to\n"
    "`N00B_PATH`.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_UNREADABLE, "N00B-M0002", ERROR,
    "an imported module exists but cannot be read",
    "The file was found, but reading it failed. The message gives the\n"
    "reason, such as missing permission.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_UNSUPPORTED_LOCATOR, "N00B-M0003", ERROR,
    "an import uses a source locator scheme this compiler does not support",
    "Import modules by name, such as `import os.path`, or by a supported\n"
    "locator.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_OWN_NAMESPACE, "N00B-M0004", ERROR,
    "a package imports itself through its external name",
    "Inside a package, import its modules by their internal names. The\n"
    "external name is for other packages.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_ALIAS_CONFLICT, "N00B-M0005", ERROR,
    "an `import ... as` name is already used for another module",
    "Each `as` name in a module must refer to one module. Choose a\n"
    "different name.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_MULTIPLE_MANIFESTS, "N00B-M0006", ERROR,
    "more than one manifest declares the same package",
    "A package is declared by exactly one `package` block. Remove the extra\n"
    "declaration.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_PARENT_MANIFEST_MISSING, "N00B-M0007", ERROR,
    "a subpackage is declared without a manifest for its parent package",
    "Declaring package `a.b` requires a manifest that declares package `a`.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_LIBRARY_SOURCE, "N00B-M0008", ERROR,
    "a module inside another package is imported directly",
    "Another package's modules are reached through its manifest. Import\n"
    "the package name the manifest exports, not the source module.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_EXPORTS_NOTHING, "N00B-M0009", ERROR,
    "an imported package exports nothing and has no subpackages",
    "Importing the package would give access to nothing. Add `export`\n"
    "statements to its `package` block.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_SINGLE_SUBPACKAGE, "N00B-M0010", WARNING,
    "a package exports nothing and holds a single subpackage",
    "The package only wraps one subpackage. Import the subpackage directly,\n"
    "or export names from the package.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_PLACEMENT, "N00B-M0011", ERROR,
    "an `import` appears inside a block",
    "Imports are allowed at module level, or directly inside a `when`\n"
    "branch at module level.")
N00B_DIAG(IMPORT_CYCLE_DEPENDENCY, "N00B-M0012", WARNING,
    "a compile-time value depends on a module that is part of an import cycle",
    "Modules in an import cycle are processed in a fixed order, so a\n"
    "compile-time value read from one of them may not be the final one.\n"
    "Move the value to a module outside the cycle.")
N00B_DIAG(NAME_SHADOWS_PACKAGE, "N00B-M0013", ERROR,
    "a declaration uses a name that refers to a package this module uses",
    "Rename the declaration, or import the package under another name with\n"
    "`import ... as`.")
N00B_DIAG(MANIFEST_OUTSIDE_PACKAGE, "N00B-M0014", ERROR,
    "a `package` block appears outside a source package",
    "Manifests are modules inside a source package directory; a module\n"
    "outside one cannot declare packages.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_DECLARED_TWICE, "N00B-M0015", ERROR,
    "a manifest declares the same package more than once",
    "Merge the `package` blocks into one.")
N00B_DIAG(EXPORT_FILESYSTEM_RENAME, "N00B-M0016", ERROR,
    "an export renames a module that comes from the filesystem",
    "Modules found as files keep their file names. Export them without\n"
    "`as`.")
N00B_DIAG(EXPORT_PRIVATE, "N00B-M0017", ERROR,
    "a manifest exports a private declaration",
    "Only declarations visible outside their module can be exported.")
N00B_DIAG(EXPORT_NOT_FOUND, "N00B-M0018", ERROR,
    "an `export` names something that does not exist",
    "The exported name must be a module or declaration of this package.\n"
    "Check the spelling.")
N00B_DIAG(EXPORT_DUPLICATE, "N00B-M0019", ERROR,
    "the same name is exported twice to the same destination",
    "Remove the repeated `export`.")
N00B_DIAG(EXPORT_FOREIGN, "N00B-M0020", ERROR,
    "a manifest exports a declaration from another package",
    "A manifest can only export declarations of its own package.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_OTHER_OWNER, "N00B-M0021", WARNING,
    "a manifest declares a package outside its own package",
    "A manifest usually declares its own package and its subpackages.\n"
    "Declaring another package here is allowed, but easy to miss.")
N00B_DIAG(EXTERNAL_NAME_AMBIGUOUS, "N00B-M0022", ERROR,
    "a package's external name is both an export and a subpackage",
    "In a package's external view, `p.x` must mean one thing. The manifest\n"
    "exports `x` from package `p` and also declares package `p.x`. Rename\n"
    "the export or the subpackage.")
N00B_DIAG(MODULE_DIRECTORY_AMBIGUOUS, "N00B-M0023", ERROR,
    "a module file and a directory have the same name",
    "A package's names follow its files, so `x.n` next to a directory `x/`\n"
    "makes `x` mean two things. Rename the module or the directory.")
N00B_DIAG(INPUT_NOT_FOUND, "N00B-B0001", ERROR,
    "a module or file named on the command line cannot be found",
    "Pass a path to a `.n` file or the name of a module on the search path.\n"
    "The message lists the places searched.")
N00B_DIAG(INPUT_UNREADABLE, "N00B-B0002", ERROR,
    "a file named on the command line cannot be read",
    "The path exists but cannot be read as a source file, for example\n"
    "because it is a directory or permission is missing.")
N00B_DIAG(BUILD_EXTRA_OPERANDS, "N00B-B0003", ERROR,
    "`n00b build` is given more than one module or file",
    "`n00b build` compiles one program. Build each program separately.")
N00B_DIAG(INVALID_NATIVE_ROOT, "N00B-B0004", ERROR,
    "a `--native-root NAME=SYMBOL` alias cannot be registered",
    "The alias needs a qualified function name and a symbol name, and each\n"
    "name may be aliased only once.")
N00B_DIAG(OPTION_REQUIRES_LIBRARY, "N00B-B0005", ERROR,
    "`--emit-interface` is used without the `library` command",
    "Semantic interfaces are produced by `n00b library --emit-interface`.")
N00B_DIAG(INTERFACE_UNREADABLE, "N00B-B0006", ERROR,
    "a `--link-interface` file cannot be loaded",
    "The file is missing, unreadable, or not a semantic interface written\n"
    "by this toolchain.")
N00B_DIAG(INTERFACE_WRITE_FAILED, "N00B-B0007", ERROR,
    "a semantic interface file cannot be written",
    "Check that the directory exists and is writable.")
N00B_DIAG(DUPLICATE_INPUT_MODULE, "N00B-B0008", ERROR,
    "two command-line inputs name the same module",
    "Each input must be a different module. Remove one of them.")
N00B_DIAG(INVALID_INPUT_NAME, "N00B-B0009", ERROR,
    "a command-line input is neither a file path nor a module name",
    "Pass a path to a `.n` file, or a dotted module name such as\n"
    "`app.main`.")
N00B_DIAG(WORKING_DIRECTORY_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-B0010", ERROR,
    "the current directory cannot be determined",
    "n00b resolves modules relative to the current directory. It may have\n"
    "been removed, or permission to read it is missing.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_SCAN_FAILED, "N00B-B0011", ERROR,
    "the package directories cannot be scanned",
    "n00b lists the source files under each package root before building.\n"
    "A directory on the search path could not be read.")
N00B_DIAG(BUILD_TIME_RUN_FAILED, "N00B-B0012", ERROR,
    "the program run that computes compile-time values failed",
    "Programs that use `comptime()` or build-time constants are first built\n"
    "and run to compute those values. That run failed; its output appears\n"
    "above.")
N00B_DIAG(FMT_OUTPUT_ARGUMENTS, "N00B-B0013", ERROR,
    "`n00b fmt --output` is used with several inputs or with `--check`",
    "`--output` writes one formatted file, so it takes exactly one input and\n"
    "cannot be combined with `--check`.")
N00B_DIAG(FMT_WRITE_FAILED, "N00B-B0014", ERROR,
    "`n00b fmt` cannot write the formatted file",
    "Check that the file or directory is writable.")
N00B_DIAG(CONFLICTING_CPU_OPTIONS, "N00B-B0015", ERROR,
    "`--native` and `--generic` are both given",
    "`--native` tunes code for this machine's processor and `--generic`\n"
    "for any processor of the architecture. Choose one.")
N00B_DIAG(JOBS_OUT_OF_RANGE, "N00B-B0016", ERROR,
    "`--jobs` is outside 0 to 128",
    "`--jobs N` sets the number of worker threads; 0 picks a default.")
N00B_DIAG(TOOLCHAIN_GRAMMAR_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-B0017", ERROR,
    "the toolchain's n00b grammar cannot be loaded",
    "The installed toolchain is incomplete or damaged. Reinstall it, or\n"
    "check `N00B_TOOLCHAIN` with `n00b env`.")
N00B_DIAG(FFI_LITERAL_NOT_FOUND, "N00B-B0018", ERROR,
    "`--show-ffi` names an `'ffi` literal that does not exist",
    "Pass the name of a `const` initialized with an `'ffi` literal.")
N00B_DIAG(HEADER_WRITE_FAILED, "N00B-B0019", ERROR,
    "the generated C header cannot be written",
    "Check that the output directory exists and is writable.")
N00B_DIAG(COMMAND_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, "N00B-B0020", ERROR,
    "the command is not implemented yet",
    "The command parsed its inputs but has no implementation yet.")
N00B_DIAG(BUILD_FAILED, "N00B-B0021", ERROR,
    "the build stopped because of the errors above",
    "Fix the errors reported before this line and build again.")
N00B_DIAG(GENERIC_SPECIALIZATION_FAILED, "N00B-B0022", ERROR,
    "a generic function cannot be specialized for the types it is used with",
    "Building a program makes a copy of each generic function for every set\n"
    "of types it is called with. This fails when the set never ends, for\n"
    "example when a generic function calls itself with a growing type.")
N00B_DIAG(PATH_ENTRY_OUTSIDE_CWD, "N00B-B0024", ERROR,
    "a relative `N00B_PATH` entry points outside the current directory",
    "Relative `N00B_PATH` entries are resolved against the current directory\n"
    "and must stay inside it, so a build does not depend on where it starts.\n"
    "Use an absolute path for directories elsewhere.")
